.TH MTOP 1 "September 27, 2026" "mtop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mtop \- terminal system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mtop
.RB [ \-i | --interval-ms\~milliseconds ]
.RB [ --theme\~name ]
.RB [ --config\~path ]
.RB [ --once ]
.RB [ --ratty-3d ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mtop
is a terminal user interface for viewing CPU, memory, swap, disk, network,
process, uptime, and best-effort GPU information.
.PP
Without
.BR --once ,
.B mtop
enters the terminal UI and refreshes system data periodically. The default
refresh interval is 1000 milliseconds. Values below 100 milliseconds are
clamped by the interactive collector. Unsupported or unavailable metrics are
shown as unavailable or reported as warnings; they do not prevent the monitor
from starting when the common system provider can run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i , " " --interval-ms " " milliseconds
Set the refresh interval in milliseconds. The default is 1000. Interactive
refreshes are limited to the 100\-10000 millisecond range.
.TP
.BI --theme\~name
Select a built-in color theme: \fBneon\fR (default), \fBamber\fR, or \fBmono\fR.
.TP
.BI --config\~path
Read configuration from the specified TOML file. A missing file uses built-in
defaults; a file that exists but is malformed causes an error and a non-zero
exit. No configuration file is created automatically, and the current
implementation does not search a default path when this option is omitted.
.TP
.B --once
Collect one snapshot, print a concise text report containing CPU, memory, and
process counts, and exit without entering the interactive terminal UI.
.TP
.B --ratty-3d
Emit Ratty Graphics Protocol panel frames for the Ratty terminal emulator.
This option is opt-in and has no effect in terminals that do not support Ratty's
graphics protocol.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B q, Esc
Quit the monitor.
.TP
.B ?, h
Toggle the keyboard help overlay.
.TP
.B r
Request an immediate refresh.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume periodic collection.
.TP
.B +, =
Increase the refresh interval by 100 milliseconds, up to 10 seconds.
.TP
.B -
Decrease the refresh interval by 100 milliseconds, down to 100 milliseconds.
.TP
.B j, Down
Select the next process.
.TP
.B k, Up
Select the previous process.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The optional configuration file is TOML and is read only when supplied with
.BR --config .
Supported fields are:
.PP
.nf
interval_ms = 1000
theme = "neon"
process_limit = 25
process_sort = "cpu"
show_gpu = true
.fi
.PP
The built-in defaults are used when no file is supplied or the specified file
does not exist. Command-line values for
.B --interval-ms
and
.B --theme
override the corresponding TOML values.
.SH PLATFORM AND GPU CAVEATS
The common collector uses the Rust sysinfo dependency, so metric availability
depends on the operating system, permissions,
and the data exposed by the host. This repository's current runtime evidence
is native-tested on macOS; Linux and BSD-family targets are compile-only or
otherwise unverified here. Do not infer runtime support from a successful
cross-compilation.
.PP
GPU reporting is optional and best effort. The default build does not require a
GPU provider. The optional
.B gpu-nvidia
feature provides the NVIDIA backend only on supported Linux builds; hardware,
drivers, and NVML availability are still required. Other GPU providers are not
currently exposed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested snapshot or interactive session completed normally.
.TP
.B non-zero
An argument, configuration, terminal, or collection setup error prevented
normal completion.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mtop
Start the interactive monitor with default settings.
.TP
.B mtop --interval-ms 250 --theme amber
Refresh four times per second using the amber theme.
.TP
.B mtop --config ~/.config/mtop/config.toml
Read settings from an explicit TOML configuration file.
.TP
.B mtop --once
Print one snapshot for a script or health check.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR htop (1)
